    <innerclass refid="classapi_1_1v2_1_1JsonHelper" prot="public">api::v2::JsonHelper</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceapi">api</innernamespace>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2">api::v2</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Conversions between JsonCpp, jsoncons and response strings. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Declares the JsonHelper class, a stateless toolbox with three static functions: one wraps a text message into a JsonCpp object with a &quot;Message&quot; key, and two others turn JsonCpp or jsoncons values into pretty-printed strings. All constructors and assignments are deleted, so the class exists purely as a namespace for its helper functions.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: The codebase uses two JSON libraries: JsonCpp for HTTP response bodies (via Drogon) and jsoncons for validation work. This helper bridges them and gives the rest of the server one consistent way to build simple status/error bodies and to turn JSON values into readable text. Without it, each caller would duplicate the wrapping and stringifying logic and the output shape could drift.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Static member functions: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/static#Static_member_functions">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/static#Static_member_functions</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Deleted functions (= delete): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/member_functions#Deleted_functions">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/member_functions#Deleted_functions</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Function overloading (two stringify versions): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/overload_resolution">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/overload_resolution</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
